
Comic Craft – Project Development Phase

Since Comic Craft is a small project, the Development Phase focuses on building the main features identified during the planning and design stages.

1. Purpose

The purpose of this phase is to turn the approved design into a working Comic Craft application.

2. Development Activities

1. Create the Project

Set up the project files and folders.

Configure the development environment.

Connect the required database.


2. Develop the User Interface

Create the basic screens:

Home page

Comic creation page

Comic editor

My Comics page

Preview page


3. Develop the Comic Editor

The main feature of Comic Craft should allow users to:

Create comic panels.

Add characters.

Add backgrounds.

Add speech bubbles.

Enter dialogue.

Move and resize elements.

Edit or remove elements.


4. Implement Save Function

Users should be able to save their comics and continue editing them later.

5. Implement Preview/Export

Users should be able to preview their completed comic and, if included in the project scope, download it as an image or PDF.

6. Connect the Database

Store basic information such as:

User details

Comic title

Comic content

Saved projects


7. Basic Error Handling

The system should display simple messages when:

Required information is missing.

A comic cannot be saved.

An invalid action is performed.


3. Development Process

